Validate local Antithesis setup

Compose configs:
Runs docker-compose locally and watches for the setup-complete event to confirm
instrumentation is working. After setup-complete is detected, discovers test
commands from /opt/antithesis/test/v1 inside the running containers and
validates their structure.

Before starting anything, validate resolves the compose file twice — with your
shell and under a scrubbed environment matching the hermetic Antithesis
environment — and fails if any ${VAR} resolves differently, catching setups that
only work locally because a value came from your shell. Use
--allow-compose-divergence to downgrade that to a warning.

Test commands are discovered by scanning /opt/antithesis/test/v1 from each
running container for {test_name}/{command} entries. Test commands are validated
to have recognized prefixes and at least one driver or anytime test command when
any are present. Test commands are not executed.

The setup-complete event is watched through a temp directory bind-mounted into
each container. If your container engine runs inside a VM or on another machine
and does not share this machine's temp directory, snouty will not be able to see
the setup-complete event. Set SNOUTY_TEMP_DIR to a directory under a path the VM
shares with write access, or share this machine's temp directory with the VM.

Kubernetes configs:
Runs docker.io/antithesishq/k8s-validator against the manifests/ directory to
perform static analysis of the manifests. --timeout, --keep-running, and
--allow-compose-divergence have no effect here (no workloads or containers are
started, and there is no docker-compose config to render).

Examples:
  snouty validate ./config
  snouty validate ./config --timeout 5m
  snouty validate ./k8s-config

Next, launch the config with `snouty launch --config ./config`. A Kubernetes
config needs the Kubernetes launcher:
`snouty launch --launcher basic_k8s_test --config ./k8s-config`.

Usage: snouty validate [OPTIONS] <CONFIG>

Arguments:
  <CONFIG>
          Path to config directory containing either docker-compose.yaml or a
          manifests/ subdirectory (Kubernetes manifests)

Options:
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Maximum time to wait for containers to start and reach setup-complete.
          A duration is a whole number with an h, m or s unit, or several in
          that order, such as 90s, 5m or 1h30m; a bare number is not permitted
          
          [default: 2m]

      --keep-running
          Leave containers running after validation for manual inspection

      --allow-compose-divergence
          Warn instead of failing when docker-compose.yaml renders differently
          in the hermetic Antithesis environment than it does on this machine

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
